      ],
      "source": "https://casselman.sites.bciti.info/en/my-municipality/living-in-casselman/history"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The river that borders Casselman was originally called the Petite-Nation when Martin first settled there.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://casselman.sites.bciti.info/en/my-municipality/living-in-casselman/history"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A sawmill and dam sprang up on the riverbank in 1844, launching the town’s timber trade.",
